id: pm-github-r14n
title: Packed projection package installation exceeds its deadline on the shared development host
description: "During #202 verification at main 03c3059, the unchanged packed projection test timed out in package install before its import assertions. Two repaired-fixture attempts, including one using the existing public npm cache, hit the same unchanged 45-second child deadline. This is a local validation limitation, not evidence of import corruption or a cleanup regression. Investigate installation cost and shared-host contention without raising command/test deadlines, weakening coverage, or using live provider data. Final-head hosted npm/Bun Node22/26 evidence is tracked separately by pm-github-mes8."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,fixtures,follow-up
created_at: "2026-11-06T12:54:44.193Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-10T03:10:37.977Z"
author: codex-astra
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce and isolate package-install cost with synthetic packed consumers; retain the existing deadlines and assertions; document comparison with the hosted matrix.
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T13:59:53.518Z",codex-astra,"A later full focused rerun completed successfully through pm test: import-projection 6/6, including the packed npm/native Bun consumer, with unchanged 45-second child and 600-second test deadlines. No installation or timeout implementation was changed to obtain this pass. Earlier baseline and repaired timeouts remain valid evidence of an intermittent shared-host validation limit; no definitive resource/registry root cause is claimed."
  "2026-11-10T03:10:33.766Z",codex-agent,"Additional unchanged-code packed-fixture evidence from PR #229: npm run release:check passed all 1800 executed tests, including the built-package selector CLI case. The sequential bun run release:check test phase reported 1799 passed, 1 failed, 2 existing SDK skips. Its sole failure was test/import-selection.test.ts:250 package-install setup: spawnSync returned null rather than 0 under the existing 45000 ms child limit (47799 ms for the whole test). The current assertion does not retain an error code or signal, so a definitive timeout/resource/registry cause is not claimed. An isolated recheck with temporary NODE_V8_COVERAGE and isolated Git identity passed 1/1 in 37276 ms using node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"built package dispatch advertises and honors selectors and limits through the real CLI\" test/import-selection.test.ts. No deadline, assertion, fixture installer or production selector code was changed. Reusing this existing intermittent packed-installation follow-up instead of creating another item."
